# Pairs with EveryCommittedKeyReadable, and restores the gate's arm order from
# before issue #4428: the Indeterminate arm is tested ahead of the orphan
# guard. A late reshard orphan bucket on a leaf that has already applied the
# commit terminal is then hidden for as long as the registry reports
# Indeterminate, and nothing guarantees either that the mask lifts or that the
# orphan is discarded. Every such key was observed post-saga before its orphan
# arrived, so the defect is visible only to the boxed form of the property:
# the reader is served the committed value, then refused it for ever.
MODULE: EveryCommittedKeyReadableIndeterminateFirst
TARGET: EveryCommittedKeyReadable
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the gate tests its Indeterminate arm ahead of the orphan guard, so a late orphan hides a committed key for as long as the registry is masked

--- FIND
    THEN IF AlreadyTerminal(t, k) THEN Projected(t, k)
         ELSE IF RegistryView(t) = "indeterminate" THEN "hidden"
         ELSE IF SurfaceViaGate(t, k) THEN "post"
         ELSE Projected(t, k)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the Indeterminate arm is tested ahead of the orphan guard.
    THEN IF RegistryView(t) = "indeterminate" THEN "hidden"
         ELSE IF SurfaceViaGate(t, k) THEN "post"
         ELSE Projected(t, k)
--- END